// Muxr dev-rig zellij config.
//
// Intentionally minimal: zellij fills in its built-in defaults for every section
// we omit (keybinds, plugin aliases, themes, web client, …). What we pin is an
// empty `load_plugins` block and the two start-up pane settings at the end.
//
// zellij's bundled default config loads background plugins through
// `load_plugins` (in 0.45.1: `load_plugins { "zellij:link" }`, which makes
// terminal file-paths clickable). Such a plugin loads on every new session and
// surfaced as a stray pane in app-created sessions. An explicit empty block
// keeps it — and any other background plugin — from loading, on 0.45.1 and
// 0.46.0 alike.
//
// Installed by entrypoint.sh on every boot. The config dir (/root/.config/zellij)
// is a persisted named volume in compose.yaml, so a build-time COPY alone would
// only seed a fresh volume and miss pre-existing ones — hence the entrypoint
// (re)install.
load_plugins {
}

// zellij opens a floating plugin pane on a version's first run: release notes
// (seen on 0.46.0 in this rig) or start-up tips. In a rig whose sessions a
// phone attaches to, that is one more pane to dismiss. With the pane, zellij
// 0.46.0 also logged two failed background commands here; with these settings
// it logs none. Both settings load on 0.45.1 and 0.46.0.
show_release_notes false
show_startup_tips false
